  "preamble": "Implosivization of a voiced velar stop: [g] becomes the implosive [ɠ]. Velar implosives are cross-linguistically rarer than labial and coronal ones, but in Sindhi and Saraiki Middle Indo-Aryan initial g- and geminate -gg- regularly gave ɠ (Masica 1991, Shackle 1976), alongside ɓ, ɗ (Saraiki ᶑ) and ʄ. Wikipedia notes that the origin of the Saraiki implosives is on the whole the same as in Sindhi, from the older series of plain voiced stops.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Implosivization, Glottalization",
